Subject: [PATCH] arch/lkl: select HAVE_ARCH_PREL32_RELOCATIONS

The kernel's exported-symbol table (`__ksymtab`) is built with 64-bit
absolute pointers by default (`struct kernel_symbol::value = &foo`).
When `liblkl.a` is statically linked into a PIE executable on AArch64
with `ld.lld` (NDK Bionic toolchain) every such entry triggers
`R_AARCH64_ABS64` relocations, which lld rejects:

  ld.lld: error: relocation R_AARCH64_ABS64 cannot be used against
                 symbol 'init_task'; recompile with -fPIC
  ...
  ld.lld: error: too many errors emitted, stopping now

Mainline `arch/arm64/` (and `arch/x86_64/`) select
`HAVE_ARCH_PREL32_RELOCATIONS`, which switches `EXPORT_SYMBOL()` to
emit each ksymtab entry as a 32-bit PC-relative offset
(`R_AARCH64_PREL32` / `R_X86_64_PC32`). Those relocations are PIE-safe.

LKL runs as a userspace library on top of POSIX hosts (x86_64, aarch64,
riscv64), and every supported host linker (ld.bfd, ld.gold, ld.lld)
handles PREL32. Selecting the option is safe and resolves the link
failure for both Android Bionic and glibc cross builds with strict
linkers.

---
 arch/lkl/Kconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/lkl/Kconfig b/arch/lkl/Kconfig
--- a/arch/lkl/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/lkl/Kconfig
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ config LKL
 	select GENERIC_STRNCPY_FROM_USER
 	select GENERIC_STRNLEN_USER
 	select HAVE_ARCH_KASAN
+	select HAVE_ARCH_PREL32_RELOCATIONS
 	select TRACING

 config LKL_FUZZING
